Z||000004||Raydar||11-10-2001||05:21 PM||||I'm thinking clutch hydraulics and/or pedal.<BR>First thing... The clutch should sit at least an inch higher than the brake. <BR>Since it's an 85, you might have the weaker pedal. The early ones were notorious for bending.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000005||TRiAD||11-10-2001||05:57 PM||||Yeah, it sits up a good 1/2"...||||reg||1
Z||000006||fropuff||11-10-2001||06:18 PM||||Sorry about your misfortune.  That sucks.  If it comes down to you needing a new tranny, Fierodave posted a few days ago about one from an'85 GT, 4 speed, with 90K miles.  The car was wrecked, and he assumes that the tranny is okay.  He was looking for $100 with no warranty.  Good luck.||||reg||1
