Z||000008||artherd||11-10-2001||07:35 PM||||STEEL PEDAL  STEEL PEDAL  STEEL PEDAL!!!!<P>Your pedal is bent man. Easier item to replace though, get it from Rodney, he's our lifesaver!<P>PS: Welcome to the world of Fiero ownership (goofy slightly sarcastic crazy man grin)<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000009||Fierowrecker||11-10-2001||08:32 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by TRiAD:<BR><B>Thanks, I was pretty miffed earlier, but stuff happens. <P>I'm fairly certain the tranny (and engine) are OK, I think it's either something with the clutch or just as likely the linkage/shifter...<P>Thanks!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hey Triad!<BR>I think you are having clutch problems too...<BR>Best to bleed out and run in new fluid (DOT 3)...<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000010||FieroMaster88||11-10-2001||09:10 PM||||I would say it is a bad master or slave cylinder.  Try replacing them...or look for any leaks in the system ANYWHERE!  I hope this helps a little.  Good luck!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jamessig.jpg">                   <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster88<BR>Not your ordinary 88 coupe!||||reg||1
Z||000011||Matthew_Fiero||11-10-2001||09:22 PM||||Since when did Rodney supply pedals?<BR>i looked on his site and couldn't find them||||reg||1
Z||000012||Mach10||11-10-2001||09:28 PM||||Bleeed! BLLLLEEEEEEEED!!!!<P>If the car creeps, then the clutch isn't disengaging... Find the leak/air bubble. Probably one of the Master, slave cylinders, possibly one of the hydraulic fittings.<P>Good luck!||||reg||10
Z||000013||85ZainoGT||11-10-2001||09:43 PM||||gimney christmas triad, what have you done to my car??? it worked fine for me... I had the shifting problem once 2 months ago about,but it was for like  minutes... <P>------------------<BR>Paul Ventimiglia<BR>1987 Gold GT 2.8L<BR>All the options :)<BR>  pics are coming :)||||reg||1
Z||000014||SLYGUY||11-10-2001||10:36 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroMaster88:<BR><B>I would say it is a bad master or slave cylinder.  Try replacing them...or look for any leaks in the system ANYWHERE!  I hope this helps a little.  Good luck!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The more I read about your problem the more obvious it was. You know what you got?<P>AIR!!!!!<P>If the pedal rises to about 1/2 inch above the brake pedal and doesn't seize or drop lifeless to the floor your master cylinder might still be okay.<P>I had the exact same symptoms including the creeping and your clutch is not disengaging. <P>Buy a Mityvac brake bleeder vacuum pump, a big bottle of DOT 3 brake fluid.<BR>Be sure to follow Archie's way to bleed the system. Type in Archie clutch in the search.<P>Good Luck<P>Sly||||reg||1
Z||000015||cid_colada||11-11-2001||12:00 AM||||About the master cylinder, get down on the floor so that you can see where the rod goes into it at, and pull the rubber boot back away from the wall. if there is any moisture in there then you need to replace it. Another thing is to take the cap off, have somebody SLOWLY depress the pedal, and watch to see if the fluid level rises... if so then you need to flush the system... CLOG.<BR>Hope this helps...<P>Matt<P>Black 84 SE||||reg||1
Z||000016||TRiAD||11-11-2001||12:38 AM||||Uh, guys?<BR>So, I need to check<BR>-Clutch master and slave cylinders for leaks<BR>-bleed the system, check for clogs and/or air, use better fluid<BR>-check the clutch pedal for a bend<P>I also need to replace the shifter mechanism. <P>...Gonna be a fun couple of weeks...<P>Thanks all!<P>(but ain't she pretty?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://communities.msn.com/_Secure/0PQBlO30UbVXblRDE93zkbJ*AbWuOFSwEgUNSQksgimNRwyPdIgVAErC*lxq8VzsyBlz*DohX40LrIT7bjgzsbEpwTOgYO0ja/1985-Signature0.gif">   <BR><B><I><FONT COLOR="blue">Project MR1 ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</B></I></FONT><p>[This message has been edited by TRiAD (edited 11-11-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000017||TRiAD||11-11-2001||04:07 PM||||UPDATE, the sequel...<P>OK, it worked a bit last night and this morning; thought I could fake it...<P>The creep is getting worse...It seems like the clutch cylinder(s) is/are going to be the main culprit(s). <P><FONT COLOR="red">the car is parked till I can get it properly diagnosed/fixed.</FONT><P>I'm VERY disappointed. I spent all the money I had for now just buying the car and getting it home. I really need transportation, and have no way to fix this yet. <P>I'm going to call Fiero Bob in the morning, and see what he has and suggests. I'm going to try to get clutch master/slave cylinders, shifter mechanism, and maybe a new pedal.<P>If anyone has some parts they don't need, and wants to help, give me a call and we can tear into it.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ||||reg||1
